		"outline": "a fountain of arching fronds on one straight column, with offshoots (suckers) at the foot",
		"habit": "mature palm 15 to 25 m tall, crown 6 to 10 m wide; height to width about 2.5 to 1. Crown about a third of the height; clear trunk about two thirds. Widest at the crown, near the top. Outline: a fountain of arching fronds on one straight column, with offshoots (suckers) at the foot.",
		"branching": "none. Fronds rise in a spiral from the trunk top; inner fronds steep, outer ones arching and drooping; a skirt of dead fronds below.",
		"leaves": "pinnate fronds 4 to 6 m long, rachis smooth, flattened, pale yellow-green, unjointed. 100 to 200 leaflets per side, 20 to 40 cm long and 1 to 2 cm wide (fifteen to thirty times as long as wide), stiff, V-folded lengthwise (induplicate), set singly and in groups of two to three along the rachis at different angles, so the frond looks bristly. The lowest leaflets are long stiff yellow spines. Grey-green and waxy on both faces; no terminal leaflet pair broader than the rest.",
